1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,584
Enterprise permissions change every day.

2
00:00:02,584 --> 00:00:04,444
Access reviews don't.

3
00:00:04,444 --> 00:00:13,307
Bastion is a fleet of three governed agents that audits the Google Cloud project it runs inside — reading production IAM read-only.

4
00:00:13,307 --> 00:00:15,940
It can ask a human to review a permission.

5
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:17,655
It cannot change one.

6
00:00:17,655 --> 00:00:27,605
It's deployed on Google's managed agent stack, not a local script — and building it there surfaced a real defect in Google's own ADK, which we reported upstream.

7
00:00:27,605 --> 00:00:30,648
Everything after this is live.

8
00:00:33,648 --> 00:00:37,166
An approved enterprise event opens the investigation.

9
00:00:37,166 --> 00:00:43,461
Pub/Sub and Eventarc give it a durable inbox with a lease, so the work survives a restart.

10
00:00:43,461 --> 00:00:48,576
This deployment is event-triggered — there is no recurring schedule in this snapshot.

11
00:00:52,576 --> 00:01:01,409
The Access Auditor reads production IAM with read-only authority — sixty-two live bindings on this route.

12
00:01:01,409 --> 00:01:07,635
Deterministic rules, not the model, produce the findings: three, across two owning teams.

13
00:01:07,635 --> 00:01:13,000
Raw principals, roles and bindings stop inside that tool.

14
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,668
Gemini 3.5 Flash writes a bounded rationale for one finding.

15
00:01:21,668 --> 00:01:25,235
It cannot add, drop, re-score or redirect one.

16
00:01:25,235 --> 00:01:32,744
Every field is checked against the tool's canonical output; if they disagree, the investigation fails closed.

17
00:01:36,744 --> 00:01:42,366
The Escalation Agent holds no IAM read role at all, and no model.

18
00:01:42,366 --> 00:01:50,422
It delivers count-only reviews to the teams that own them — two findings to security-engineering, one durable review record.

19
00:01:50,422 --> 00:01:53,1000
Completion requires a receipt from every required delivery.

20
00:01:56,1000 --> 00:02:00,850
A human approved an exception for platform-infra.

21
00:02:00,850 --> 00:02:07,697
Three days later, across redeployments and restarts, the matching finding was suppressed and that team was not paged again.

22
00:02:07,697 --> 00:02:13,968
The decision was remembered across a real elapsed gap — not re-derived by a model.

23
00:02:17,968 --> 00:02:22,519
Separation is enforced by IAM, not prompt wording.

24
00:02:22,519 --> 00:02:28,925
The Auditor identity performs this read; the Escalation identity is denied the same call.

25
00:02:28,925 --> 00:02:34,144
This denial is reproduced by impersonation, not captured mid-investigation.

26
00:02:37,144 --> 00:02:42,369
A compromised authorized caller sends an injection through the Auditor's own A2A surface.

27
00:02:42,369 --> 00:02:45,373
The deployed callback refuses it before Gemini.

28
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:51,232
The task fails closed, and zero model submissions, completions or tool calls follow.

29
00:02:54,232 --> 00:03:00,488
Cloud Trace shows one connected chain — twenty-two spans across the Runtime and both workers.

30
00:03:00,488 --> 00:03:08,684
Separately, a payload-free audit joins every event under one investigation ID, retained a year in europe-west4.

31
00:03:08,684 --> 00:03:12,040
The trace expires; the audit is the compliance record.

32
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:27,976
All of it runs privately on Google Cloud — managed Agent Runtime, Gateway, Registry and Memory Bank, with Cloud Run, Firestore, Pub/Sub and Vertex AI behind an IAM-private boundary.

33
00:03:29,976 --> 00:03:37,305
Bastion turns real IAM into remembered, department-owned action — without ever giving an agent write access.

34
00:03:37,305 --> 00:03:43,530
The ADK defect it surfaced is now an open issue upstream, confirmed by a Google maintainer.

35
00:03:43,530 --> 00:03:47,592
Every claim here has a proof boundary in the public repository.
